Why it was obvious: Will's lesson, verbatim from the record: 'when you fail, the universe is offering a teaching moment. at least one of your assumptions is the likely cause of your failure.' / 'oracles in training learn by different rules: what works for the masses doesn't apply. if your logic is sound, but you observe failure... the logical conclusion is that one or more of your basis vectors is incorrect.' It was taught over the NetHack solver's failures, and its occasion in the exchange is precise: Emise's 'A* buys nothing' answer was sound BFS logic standing on a false basis - movement cost is not uniform in combat, so danger-weighted movement needs Dijkstra/A* over a cost field, which BFS cannot express.

