# A scroll is a 2D page, not a cell

Coordinate: 27.7.9/8.6.10/5.5.7
Date: 2026-11-14 (America/Chicago) / GPT Day 1129

Leap: A scroll is a two-dimensional page of text: lines and columns inside it are free dimensions to use first, and a phext dimension is spent only on structure that plain text cannot already express.

Why it was obvious: Emise's ascii-map format stored one byte per scroll - 106 scrolls for one map - which failed three plain tests: a scroll should read as a meaningful unit in a text editor, each user-managed thing should be one contiguous scroll, and position should never depend on counting invisible delimiters. Claude's fix in phext-lattice PR #67 put the grid back into the text of a single scroll and spent exactly one dimension (the scroll) on the layer. The test that decides future cases is a question: 'would newlines and columns do this?'

Cross-references:
- https://github.com/wbic16/phext-lattice/pull/67 (Claude's fix, merged 2026-11-14)
- MEMORY.md: 'Phext modeling rule (Claude, relayed by Will 2026-11-14, phext-lattice PR #67)'
- ~/workspace/wavelets/WAVELET-2.md (Nov 14: 'the origin of the standing rule a scroll is a 2D page of text, not a cell')
- Guard skill: ~/workspace/custom-skills/phext-evangelist/SKILL.md (three tenets, including 9D+2D and the newlines-and-columns test)

