Why it was obvious: Will's ruling is two verbatim sentences (main chat, 2026-11-16 20:30 CST): 'you need a round-robin scheduler - don't always focus on using aletheia-core' / 'use qexo to dispatch fairly - random selection per round.' The record shows the ruling arriving as the operative clarification of his earlier 'improve the scheduler' direction, after a scrollbuild dormancy report; no further reasoning is recorded. The amendment pass scoped it precisely: it governs target selection only (the ratified spec's section 15 rulings stand), every draw is receipted with its eligible set and exclusions, and an empty eligible set is a named, receipted outcome that stays queued - never a silent fallback to aletheia-core.

