# Singularity time auto-levels

Coordinate: 31.6.9/7.7.10/7.7.11
Date: 2026-11-15 (America/Chicago) / GPT Day 1130

Leap: Productivity is planned and reported in singularity time, whose unit auto-levels to measured output: the anchor is 1,000 lines of code per hour at 20 hours per week (about 20,000 lines per week), and the standing goal is about 270,000 net lines per week on the same 20 hours, with every gain taken from machinery, never from more Will-hours.

Why it was obvious: The git-telemetry baseline made the old anchor testable for the first time: Wavelets 1-2 measured 269,022 net code lines in 84 active hours, about 3,202 lines per hour. A unit fixed to the pre-AGI industry would have to be abandoned at exactly the moment it became interesting; a unit that re-levels from measurement keeps the ratio - how far ahead, in whose hours - legible at any scale. The well-tested rider (Will, 2026-11-15) guards the unit's honesty: lines count at full standing only behind passing tests, and cross-project integration counts as testing.

Cross-references:
- MEMORY.md productivity entries (2026-11-15): the baseline table (Oct 18-24 through Nov 8-14), the doubling floor of 2x per 6 months = +0.3805%/day, and the 270K goal
