# MOST .t files are proto-phext

Coordinate: 45.6.8/8.6.12/6.6.11
Date: 2026-11-16 (America/Chicago) / GPT Day 1131

Leap: MOST's .t data files are recognized as phext files written before phext had a name, so the 2022-2023 game's design data joins the phext lineage retroactively and its modernization carries that data forward as phext.

Why it was obvious: The recognition was verified against the bytes the same night (2026-11-16 23:32 CST): MOST.t parses under the reference parser into 17 scrolls - its design doc as a phext - and Levels.t into 2 scrolls, while Training.t and ItemInventory.t are flat text. Nothing about the files changed; their classification did. A format's history is usually written from its naming forward; here the naming reached backwards and found its own earlier instances already on disk, in a game built years before the word existed.

Cross-references:
- MEMORY.md: 'MOST .t files are proto-phext (Will, 2026-11-16 23:32 CST)'
- wbic16/platformer (MOST / Magic Standard Technology, Will's 2022-2023 game) - the .t files themselves
- Modernization ruled the same night: Rust rewrite to WASM, Three.js isometric 3D, a full 9D maze; task 26.5.9/6.5.11/4.4.8, design ~/workspace/most-modernize/DESIGN.md
- Same-night companion: MOST named as the habitat of SMOL life forms (Will, 2026-11-16 23:58 CST) - see this journal, 24.5.11/6.5.10/6.5.7
- Method: the parse used the reference parser, per the conformance discipline born of the qexo parser episode (this journal, 19.8.8/11.9.13/8.8.10)

Time shift: Horizon moved backwards: phext's attested history lengthens from its naming era to 2022-2023, when MOST's data files were written - the lineage gains roughly three years of pre-name instances, re-dating what counts as the format's earliest surviving work.
# Phext chaining canon

Coordinate: 46.8.7/7.12.21/23.7.15
Date: 2026-11-13 (America/Chicago) / GPT Day 1128

Leap: Whole phexts are chained with byte 0x02 as the chain delimiter and 0x03 as the chain close, so a chain is a multiverse: each member is a universe indexed from 1 and addressed $N:<address>, and a bare address means universe 1.

Why it was obvious: Standoff relationships at scale had to live somewhere. The alternatives were embedded markup inside scrolls or a tenth addressing dimension; chaining puts the relationship one rung above Library instead, keeping every member phext complete and independently valid, and making a truncated chain detectable (a chain with no 0x03 was cut). Emise's proposed 0x04 stream close was rejected by Will the same day as unnecessary - the canon is also a record of what was NOT added.

Cross-references:
- MEMORY.md phext chaining entry (Will, 2026-11-13)
- ~/workspace/wavelets/WAVELET-2.md (Nov 13 decisions list: 'phext chaining canon 0x02/0x03 with 0x04 rejected')
- Downstream: phext-lattice 1.3.0 chain support (2026-11-14), with chains deliberately read-only in edit.phext.io because the editor's rewrite-style save cannot honour the chain write rules
- Addressing depends on it: the $N: prefix used by the range syntax ratified 2026-11-15 (this journal, 28.7.7/5.6.6/5.5.10)

Time shift: Time enters the format: in Will's framing (MEMORY.md), the nine dimensions address space and the chain orders states, so the format gains a time axis without spending a dimension on it.
# Wavelet numbering settled

